// Plugin: no-decorators — any decorator (legacy OR Stage-3/TC39).
// Decorators are NOT erasable: node's type-stripping (tsx / `node --experimental-strip-types`) has no
// decorator runtime, so a decorator throws at runtime. Critically, the `erasableSyntaxOnly` tsc flag
// is SILENT on decorators — the compiler will not catch this, so the lint IS the gate. Use function
// composition / zod validation, never decorator-based DI or `reflect-metadata`.
// Refs: spine/typescript-style.md §5 (erasableSyntaxOnly forbidden set).
language js

JsDecorator() as $node where {
  register_diagnostic(span=$node, message="decorators are not erasable — tsx/node type-stripping has no decorator runtime (runtime error), and the erasableSyntaxOnly compiler flag does NOT catch them. Use function composition / zod, not decorators. See spine/typescript-style.md §5.")
}
